# ==============================================================================
# .dockerignore for KnowLayer (Company-Bot)
# ==============================================================================
# REASONING:
# The Docker build context is sent as a tar archive from the host machine to the
# Docker daemon. Ignoring unnecessary files drastically speeds up build times,
# reduces container image size, and prevents sensitive credentials from leaking into layers.
# ==============================================================================

# 1. PYTHON BYTECODE & CACHES
# REASONING: Bytecode compiled on Windows host will not work inside Linux container
# and bloats the build context unnecessarily.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# 2. LOCAL VIRTUAL ENVIRONMENTS
# REASONING: The host virtual environment (.venv) contains Windows binaries and
# libraries. The container must install its own Linux-compatible packages via pip.
.venv/
env/
venv/
ENV/

# 3. GIT & VERSION CONTROL
# REASONING: .git history is heavy and not needed at runtime inside the production container.
.git/
.gitignore
.github/

# 4. SENSITIVE CREDENTIALS & SECRETS
# REASONING: Never bake .env secrets directly into the image layers.
# Secrets should be injected at runtime via docker-compose (env_file / environment).
.env
*.pem
*.key

# 5. EPHEMERAL RUNTIME & LOCAL DATA
# REASONING: Local database files and cache should not overwrite container state.
# These will be mounted as persistent Docker volumes at runtime instead.
instance/*.db3
instance/*.db
conversation_logs/
.chroma/
cache/

# 6. IDE & SYSTEM FILES
# REASONING: Host operating system and editor metadata irrelevant to the Linux container.
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
